    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "Blocking review at head 12cb623c: runtime clean Stage 7.15 fresh start shows 0 REP, canonical initial baseline is 1. Please do not merge or claim PASS_CANDIDATE. Source-level audit: `claimFreshStart()` calls `resetStage715FreshState()`, then `start(..., \"fresh\")` invokes that reset again. The baseline transfer result is ignored by `start()`; the controller immediately saves the checkpoint even if initialization failed, while `initializeStage715InitialRepBaseline` skips on resume, allowing an uninitialized 0-REP save to persist. Also `ui-boot.js` assigns `S.rep = 0` outside protected State.rep write API. These are code-proven issues/risk paths but are not yet the confirmed runtime cause. Add RED-first production-boot regression with real guarded State.transferRep and separate init/render checks, capture the real transfer result/reason, State.rep before and after, initial flag and ledger; fix only the proven cause, prevent valid checkpoint from silently persisting failed baseline, then rerun one native-browser-tab full Nastya and Oleg runtime including reload and exact-once. Keep PR draft; Atom 7 blocked.",
