    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## Summary\n- Reveal Oleg escape votes one at a time from a persisted randomized sequence and resume from the correct vote after reload.\n- Randomize Nastya's first four vote sides while preserving existing vote intervals and the 3:2 outcome.\n- Keep Core as the owner of vote settlement and repair the split-store terminal-state handoff.\n- Recover an Oleg REP settlement from its canonical ledger actionId if the state flag write was interrupted; preserve insufficient-funds and other economy failures without fabricating a transfer.\n- Add regression coverage for distinct Game.__S and Game.UI.S, Core settlement, Stage outcome messages/card, retry, second escape, and exactly-once REP recovery.\n\n## Validation\n- RED-first lifecycle regression reproduced the split-store 2:3 Core settlement followed by a blocked Stage outcome.\n- Focused Oleg split-store lifecycle regression: PASS.\n- Oleg lifecycle test: PASS.\n- Node syntax checks and git diff --check: PASS.\n- Paired vote-controller source/docs files match. state.js had unrelated pre-existing Web/docs text drift; this patch leaves those strings unchanged.\n\n## Runtime\n- Existing origin :8766 profile remains preserved. Its visible UI shows 0 REP and the unresolved scripted Oleg escape card, but the UI does not expose its serialized Core/UI mirrors, escape flags, or REP ledger, so those exact saved fields could not be read.\n- On clean origin :8791, a normal UI start reached a blank chat/profile shell and then ordinary ambient activity, not the requested Stage 7.15 Nastya corridor. Full Nastya and Oleg runtime, reload checkpoints, visible vote intervals, and exactly-once UI messages remain unverified.\n- This draft is NOT a PASS_CANDIDATE. Keep draft for continued diagnosis. No merge, Pages, or Atom 7.",
